---
description: Mutating controllers must authorize! the record; association find is not authz
alwaysApply: true
---

# Authorize the record

Looking up through `current_user.organizations` (or similar association find) is not authorization. Controllers that mutate call `authorize!` on the record. Policy denial (`ActionPolicy::Unauthorized`) redirects to root with flash `Not authorized`. Tenant isolation via `authorized_scope.find` stays 404. Do not unify those.

```ruby
# bad
organization = current_user.organizations.find(params.require(:organization_id))
remember_organization(organization)
```

```ruby
# good
organization = Organization.find(params.require(:organization_id))
authorize! organization, with: CurrentOrganizationPolicy
remember_organization(organization)
```

`authorize :user` in ApplicationController is context wiring, not a resource check. Do not add `verify_authorized` globally.
